# The ruling: "Once your end step begins, it's too late to make a card leave your graveyard in order to cause this
# ability to trigger" (CR 603.4: an intervening "if" false as the step begins means no trigger at all). Nothing has
# left Bot1's graveyard when its turn-3 end step begins, so the stack is empty there; Bot2 then sacrifices Soul-Guide
# Lantern to exile Bot1's graveyard. Gau does not trigger late, and at Bot2's end step on turn 4 the card left on
# another turn, not "this turn", so Bot2 keeps all its life.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Sol Ring
Gau, Feral Youth
Faithless Looting
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Soul-Guide Lantern
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Soul-Guide Lantern.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Gau, Feral Youth.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Faithless Looting.Cast
[T3 Bot1.End]
? Stack.Count = 0
Bot2.Battlefield.Soul-Guide Lantern.Activate(Ability: Exile each)
[T4 Bot2.End]
? Stack.Count = 0
[T5 Bot1.Upkeep]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot2.Life = 20
